  writing:{
    type:"Task 2", min:250, time:"40 phút",
    prompt:"What do you think is the most important factor in achieving success: natural ability, hard work or luck? Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.",
    plan:["Phân tích đề: chỉ có MỘT câu hỏi, phải chọn một yếu tố và giải thích","Mở bài: paraphrase + nêu câu trả lời (hard work)","Thân 1: lý do 1 + ví dụ","Thân 2: lý do 2 + ví dụ; thừa nhận vai trò của năng khiếu/may mắn","Kết bài: nhắc lại câu trả lời"],
    model:"People have different opinions about why some individuals become successful while others do not. Some point to natural ability, and others believe that success is mainly a matter of luck. In my view, however, hard work is the most important factor.\n\nThe first reason is that talent alone is rarely enough. Many people are born with a natural ability for music, sport or mathematics, but unless they practise regularly, they will not develop it. For example, top football players usually train for several hours every day from a very young age. Without this effort, their talent would never reach a professional level.\n\nThe second reason is that hard work can help people to create their own luck. It is true that some people are lucky enough to meet the right person or be in the right place at the right time. However, people who work hard are more likely to be ready when these opportunities appear. A student who has studied English for years, for instance, will be able to accept a job offer from an international company, while a student who has not prepared will miss the chance.\n\nOf course, natural ability and luck can make the road to success easier, and I do not deny that some people are born with advantages. But these factors are outside our control, whereas effort is something everyone can choose.\n\nIn conclusion, I believe that hard work is the key to success, because it develops natural ability and allows people to make the most of lucky opportunities."
  },
  speaking:{
    tip:"Part 1 nói về bạn; Part 3 nói về con người và xã hội nói chung. Khái quát hoá bằng ‘In general, people…’, ‘Most people tend to…’, rồi thêm lý do và ví dụ. Hạ giọng ở cuối câu khi đã nói xong.",
    p1:["Do you think you are a hard-working person?","What do you do to remember new words?","Have you changed a lot since you were a child?","Who do you usually go to for advice?"],
    p1sample:{q:"What do you do to remember new words?",a:"I write new words in a small notebook with an example sentence, and I review them on the bus every morning. I also try to use them when I talk to my English-speaking friends, because if I use a word, I remember it much better."},
    cue:{t:"Describe a successful person you know.",pts:["who this person is","how you know him or her","what he or she has achieved"],end:"and explain why you think this person is successful."},
    p2sample:"I'd like to talk about my cousin Lan, who is a software engineer. We grew up in the same neighbourhood, so I've known her all my life. Lan came from quite a poor background, and nobody in our family had ever studied computing. However, she taught herself programming using free online courses when she was in high school. Later, she won a scholarship to study in Singapore, and now she works for a well-known technology company. I think she's successful not only because she has a well-paid job, but also because she uses her skills to help others. Every weekend she teaches free coding classes for children from poor families. She always says that the key to success is to keep learning, and I really agree with her.",
    p3:["Why do some people become more successful than others?","Is it more important to have a well-paid job or a job you enjoy?","How will people's lives change in the next twenty years?"],
    p3sample:{q:"Why do some people become more successful than others?",a:"In general, I think it depends on a combination of factors. Most successful people tend to work very hard and they don't give up easily. But family background also plays a role. For instance, children whose parents can pay for extra classes often have more opportunities. So I'd say effort is the most important thing, but it's easier for some people than for others."},
    phrases:["In general,…","Most people tend to…","On the whole,…","It depends on…","For instance,…","That's why…"]
  }
