  reading:{
    title:"Last-Chance Tourism", est:"khoảng 350 từ · 14 phút",
    paras:[
      "A growing number of travellers are choosing destinations because they are disappearing. Melting glaciers, damaged coral reefs and ancient towns threatened by rising sea levels have all seen a rise in visitors. Travel writers call this trend ‘last-chance tourism’.",
      "Supporters say that this kind of travel can help. Dr Elena Ruiz, a marine scientist, argues that tourists who see a damaged coral reef with their own eyes often return home with a stronger wish to protect the environment. ‘People care about places they have experienced,’ she says.",
      "Others are less positive. Professor Kenji Mori, who studies the impact of tourism, points out that most last-chance tourists travel by plane, and flights produce large amounts of carbon dioxide, which contributes to global warming. ‘The visitors are adding to the problem they come to see,’ he says.",
      "Local communities often have mixed feelings. Tourism brings jobs and income, but large numbers of visitors can damage fragile sites. Maria Costa, who runs a small guesthouse near a glacier in South America, says her business has doubled in five years. However, she worries that the paths are becoming crowded and that rubbish is being left behind.",
      "Some destinations have introduced rules to manage the situation. Popular sites may limit the number of visitors per day, charge an entrance fee that pays for conservation, or require tourists to go with a trained local guide. Mori believes these measures help, but says the best solution is for people to choose destinations closer to home."
    ],
    note:"Các nhân vật trong bài là hư cấu.",
    quiz:[
      {t:"head",text:"Câu 1–5: Hoàn thành tóm tắt. Điền MỘT TỪ trong bài."},
      {t:"gap",q:"Last-chance tourism means visiting places that are ___.",a:["disappearing"]},
      {t:"gap",q:"Examples include glaciers, coral reefs and ancient ___.",a:["towns"]},
      {t:"gap",q:"Some sites limit the number of ___ per day,",a:["visitors"]},
      {t:"gap",q:"charge an entrance ___,",a:["fee"]},
      {t:"gap",q:"or require tourists to go with a local ___.",a:["guide"]},
      {t:"head",text:"Câu 6–9: Ai nói/nghĩ điều sau? A Elena Ruiz · B Kenji Mori · C Maria Costa"},
      {q:"Her income has increased.",o:["A Elena Ruiz","B Kenji Mori","C Maria Costa"],a:2},
      {q:"Tourists may become more interested in protecting nature.",o:["A Elena Ruiz","B Kenji Mori","C Maria Costa"],a:0},
      {q:"People should travel shorter distances.",o:["A Elena Ruiz","B Kenji Mori","C Maria Costa"],a:1},
      {q:"She is worried about litter.",o:["A Elena Ruiz","B Kenji Mori","C Maria Costa"],a:2}
    ]
  },
