  writing:{
    type:"Task 1", min:150, time:"20 phút",
    prompt:"The diagram shows how rainwater is collected and used in a house. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features.",
    charts:[{type:"process",title:"Rainwater collection system",steps:["Rain falls on the roof","Gutters collect the water","A filter removes leaves and dirt","Water is stored in an underground tank","A pump sends water into the house","Used for toilets, washing machine and garden"]}],
    plan:["Mở bài: paraphrase","Overview: có mấy bước, bắt đầu và kết thúc ở đâu","Thân 1: từ mái nhà đến bể chứa","Thân 2: từ bể chứa đến nơi sử dụng","Dùng present passive + First, Next, Then, After that, Finally"],
    model:"The diagram illustrates how rainwater is collected from the roof of a house and then used for various purposes in the home.\n\nOverall, there are six main stages in the process, beginning with rain falling on the roof and ending with the water being used inside the house and in the garden.\n\nFirst, rain falls on the roof of the house and runs into gutters along the edges. The water is then carried down a pipe to a filter, where leaves and dirt are removed. After it has been filtered, the clean water is stored in a large tank, which is located under the ground.\n\nWhen the water is needed, it is sent into the house by an electric pump. Finally, it is used for a number of everyday purposes, such as flushing toilets and running the washing machine. It can also be used to water the garden. This system means that less water from the main supply is needed."
  },
  speaking:{
    tip:"Part 2: chọn ý mà bạn có nhiều điều để nói nhất, không cần là ý ‘hay’ nhất. Part 3: xác định câu hỏi đang hỏi gì (lý do? so sánh? dự đoán?) và trả lời đúng trọng tâm, đầy đủ.",
    p1:["How much water do you drink every day?","Do you like swimming?","Is water ever a problem in your city?","Do you prefer the sea or rivers and lakes?"],
    p1sample:{q:"Is water ever a problem in your city?",a:"Yes, sometimes. In the rainy season, some streets in my city flood after heavy rain, so it's difficult to travel. But in the dry season, a few areas don't get enough tap water, and people have to buy bottled water."},
    cue:{t:"Describe a river, lake or sea that you like.",pts:["where it is","how often you go there","what you do there"],end:"and explain why you like it."},
    p2sample:"The place I've chosen to talk about is West Lake in Hanoi. It's the biggest lake in the city, and it's only about fifteen minutes from my house by motorbike. I go there about once a week, usually on Sunday morning or in the late afternoon. Most of the time I cycle around the lake with my friends. The whole route is about seventeen kilometres, so it's good exercise. After that, we often sit in a café by the water and drink iced coffee. Sometimes I also go there alone to study English, because it's much quieter than my neighbourhood. What makes it special for me is the sunset. When the sun goes down, the sky and the water turn orange and pink, and it's really peaceful. It helps me relax after a busy week.",
    p3:["Why is it important to save water?","Who should be responsible for providing clean water: governments or individuals?"],
    p3sample:{q:"Why is it important to save water?",a:"I think the main reason is that clean water is limited, even though it seems unlimited when we turn on a tap. Because of climate change, many areas have more droughts than before. For example, farmers in the Mekong Delta have suffered from salt water in their rivers. So if everyone saves a little water, there will be more for drinking and farming."},
    phrases:["The place I've chosen to talk about is…","What makes it special is…","I'd like to begin by…","The main reason is that…","For example,…","So, if…, …"]
  }
