  grammar:{
    title:"Modal verbs",
    rules:[
      {h:"Khả năng & sự cho phép",use:["can: có thể (hiện tại)","could: đã có thể (quá khứ), lời đề nghị lịch sự","may/might: có lẽ (không chắc chắn)"],form:"modal + V nguyên mẫu (không có to, không thêm -s)",ex:"This building might be 200 years old.",sig:"She can swim. (không nói: She cans swim)"},
      {h:"Bắt buộc",use:["must: bắt buộc (luật lệ, người nói thấy cần)","have to: bắt buộc (quy định bên ngoài)","mustn't: cấm · don't have to: không cần"],form:"You mustn't smoke here. · You don't have to wear a uniform.",ex:"All visitors must show their tickets.",sig:"mustn't ≠ don't have to"},
      {h:"Lời khuyên",use:["should / shouldn't: nên / không nên","Rất hay dùng trong Task 2 khi nêu giải pháp"],form:"Governments should protect old buildings.",ex:"Architects should think about energy use.",sig:"Writing Task 2"}
    ],
    quiz:[
      {q:"You ___ smoke in the hospital. It's against the rules.",o:["mustn't","don't have to","might not"],a:0,e:"Cấm → mustn't."},
      {q:"Students ___ wear a uniform at university. It's optional.",o:["don't have to","mustn't","can't"],a:0,e:"Không bắt buộc → don't have to."},
      {q:"You look tired. You ___ go to bed early.",o:["should","must not","can't"],a:0,e:"Lời khuyên → should."},
      {q:"This old house ___ be over 200 years old, but I'm not sure.",o:["might","must","should"],a:0,e:"Không chắc chắn → might."},
      {q:"When I was young, I ___ swim very well.",o:["could","can","must"],a:0,e:"Khả năng trong quá khứ → could."},
      {q:"All visitors ___ show their tickets at the entrance.",o:["must","might","could"],a:0,e:"Quy định → must."},
      {q:"She ___ speak three languages.",o:["can","cans","can to"],a:0,e:"modal + V nguyên mẫu, không thêm -s."},
      {q:"___ I open the window, please?",o:["Could","Must","Should not"],a:0,e:"Lời đề nghị lịch sự."}
    ]
  },
  reading:{
    title:"The Tube Houses of Vietnam", est:"khoảng 350 từ · 14 phút",
    paras:[
      "Walk down almost any street in Hanoi or Ho Chi Minh City and you will notice a special kind of building: the tube house, or nhà ống. These houses are usually only three to five metres wide, but they can be more than twenty metres deep and four or five storeys high.",
      "One popular explanation for their shape is that, in the past, taxes were based on the width of the front of a building. Whether or not this is completely true, land in city centres has always been expensive, so families built upwards and backwards rather than sideways. The ground floor is often used as a shop or café, while the family lives on the floors above.",
      "Tube houses have clear weaknesses. Because they are joined to the houses on either side, the rooms in the middle can be dark and hot. Stairs take up a lot of space, and elderly people may find it difficult to climb to the upper floors.",
      "In recent years, however, young Vietnamese architects have found creative solutions. Many new tube houses include an open space in the centre, sometimes with plants and trees, which allows light and air to reach every room. Others use flexible walls that can be moved to make rooms bigger or smaller.",
      "Some critics say that tube houses are old-fashioned and that cities should build more tower blocks instead. I disagree. In my opinion, tube houses create lively streets where people know their neighbours, something that is often lost in large apartment buildings. With good design, they can be comfortable homes for the future."
    ],
    quiz:[
      {t:"head",text:"Câu 1–2: Chọn đáp án đúng A, B hoặc C."},
      {q:"Tube houses are usually",o:["A wide and short","B narrow and deep","C only one storey high"],a:1},
      {q:"According to paragraph B, families built upwards mainly because",o:["A tower blocks were not allowed","B land was expensive","C they wanted a better view"],a:1},
      {t:"head",text:"Câu 3–5: Nối phần đầu câu với phần cuối đúng (A–E)."},
      {q:"The ground floor is often used",o:["A because the house is joined to its neighbours.","B as a shop or café.","C allows light and air into the house.","D because stairs are expensive.","E makes the house cheaper to build."],a:1},
      {q:"The middle rooms can be dark",o:["A because the house is joined to its neighbours.","B as a shop or café.","C allows light and air into the house.","D because stairs are expensive.","E makes the house cheaper to build."],a:0},
      {q:"An open space in the centre",o:["A because the house is joined to its neighbours.","B as a shop or café.","C allows light and air into the house.","D because stairs are expensive.","E makes the house cheaper to build."],a:2},
      {t:"head",text:"Câu 6–8: Yes / No / Not Given (quan điểm của tác giả)."},
      {q:"Cities should replace tube houses with tower blocks.",o:["Yes","No","Not Given"],a:1,e:"Đoạn E: 'I disagree'."},
      {q:"Tube houses help neighbours get to know each other.",o:["Yes","No","Not Given"],a:0,e:"Đoạn E."},
      {q:"Tube houses are cheaper to build than apartments.",o:["Yes","No","Not Given"],a:2,e:"Tác giả không so sánh chi phí xây dựng."}
    ]
  },
